<heading>delete - Delete a run of a topic.</heading>

<rule/>

<heading level="2">
Usage
</heading>

<pre>
  delete TOPIC RUN
</pre>

<heading level="2">
Description
</heading>

<paragraph>
Deletes one completed run as a whole. TOPIC may be an id or a
topic name; RUN is the numeric run id as shown by list. The run
must belong to the given topic, so a run is never removed from
the wrong place. Entries inside a run are never edited — deletion
is the only way to remove a stored run, for example a discarded
test run or an accidental save.
</paragraph>

<heading level="2">
Examples
</heading>

<pre>
delete "Roman Empire" 3
  Delete run 3 of the topic Roman Empire.
</pre>

<heading level="2">
See also
</heading>

<paragraph>
list, show, new
</paragraph>
